QMK checks each USB endpoint it sets up and then ignores the answer, so GCC
16 calls the result set but unused and QMK's -Werror stops the build. This
says the result is ignored on purpose, as QMK's own code treats it, rather
than letting every warning through.

--- a/tmk_core/protocol/lufa/lufa.c
+++ b/tmk_core/protocol/lufa/lufa.c
@@ -391,6 +391,7 @@
     ConfigSuccess &= Endpoint_ConfigureEndpoint((DIGITIZER_IN_EPNUM | ENDPOINT_DIR_IN), EP_TYPE_INTERRUPT, DIGITIZER_EPSIZE, 1);
 #endif
 
+    (void)ConfigSuccess;
     usb_device_state_set_configuration(USB_DeviceState == DEVICE_STATE_Configured, USB_Device_ConfigurationNumber);
 }
 
